<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 286 0 R
/T (Mutual exclusion primitives \(locks/mutexes\) prevent data corruption by serializing critical sections. However, coarse- grained locks introduce catastrophic performance penalties: user-space thread suspension, OS kernel context switches \(futex system calls\), and cache line invalidation across cores competing for the lock variable. In distributed and concurrent systems architecture, the foundational principle is: 'The fastest lock is no lock.')
/E (Mutual exclusion primitives \(locks/mutexes\) prevent data corruption by serializing critical sections. However, coarse- grained locks introduce catastrophic performance penalties: user-space thread suspension, OS kernel context switches \(futex system calls\), and cache line invalidation across cores competing for the lock variable. In distributed and concurrent systems architecture, the foundational principle is: 'The fastest lock is no lock.')
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
